{number: 111}
{title: Wonderful Grace of Jesus}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Wonderful grace of Jesus, greater than all my sin;
How shall my tongue describe it, where shall its [G7] praise begin?
[C] Taking away my burden, setting my spirit free;
For the [D7] wonderful grace of Jesus reaches [G7] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] Wonderful the matchless grace of Jesus,
Deeper than the [G7] mighty rolling sea;
Higher than the [C] mountain, sparkling like a fountain,
All-sufficient [G7] grace for even [C] me!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Wonderful grace of Jesus, reaching to all the lost,
By it I have been pardoned, saved to the [G7] uttermost;
[C] Chains have been torn asunder, giving me liberty;
For the [D7] wonderful grace of Jesus reaches [G7] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Wonderful grace of Jesus, reaching the most defiled,
By its transforming power, making him [G7] God's dear child,
[C] Purchasing peace and heaven, for all eternity;
And the [D7] wonderful grace of Jesus reaches [G7] me.
{end_of_verse}
